        "original_id": "8cb13a2a-1cc5-52e4-a12e-120c97281eca",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Brad Elterman, Rod Stewart, David Bowie, Robert Plant, Bebe Buell, Debbie Harry, Chris Stein, Leif Garrett, Michael Jackson, Kenny Rogers\n- Bands: Blondie, Faces, Sex Pistols, the Runaways, Kiss, Queen, the Ramones, Bay City Rollers, ABBA, Boney M, The Who\n- Places: Beverly Hills, California, Hollywood\n- Topics: Rock photography, rock 'n' roll lifestyle, musical styles, hit singles\n\nFacts:\n- Brad Elterman is a professional photographer from Beverly Hills, California.\n- Brad Elterman documented the Hollywood rock 'n' roll lifestyle across pop, punk, and rock music.\n- Brad Elterman photographed artists and bands including Faces with Rod Stewart, David Bowie, Robert Plant, Sex Pistols, the Runaways, Bebe Buell, Kiss, Queen, Blondie, the Ramones, Bay City Rollers, ABBA, Boney M, Kenny Rogers, The Who, Leif Garrett, and Michael Jackson.\n- Blondie is an American rock band founded by singer Debbie Harry and guitarist Chris Stein.\n- Over the next three years, Blondie achieved hit singles including \"Call Me,\" \"Rapture,\" and \"Heart of Glass.\"\n- Blondie became known for an eclectic mix of musical styles that incorporated disco, pop, reggae, and early rap music.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
